// Title: Potential Suspicious Windows Feature Enabled - ProcCreation
// Sigma ID: c740d4cf-a1e9-41de-bb16-8a46a4f57918
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-12-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth
// Description: Detects usage of the built-in PowerShell cmdlet "Enable-WindowsOptionalFeature" used as a
//   Deployment Image Servicing and Management tool. Similar to DISM.exe, this cmdlet is used to
//   enumerate, install, uninstall, configure, and update features and packages in Windows images
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage of the features listed in the rule.
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/dism/enable-windowsoptionalfeature?view=windowsserver2022-ps
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/projfs/enabling-windows-projected-file-system
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/install-on-server
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_enable_susp_windows_optional_feature.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "Enable-WindowsOptionalFeature" and ProcessCommandLine contains "-Online" and ProcessCommandLine contains "-FeatureName") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "TelnetServer" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Internet-Explorer-Optional-amd64" or ProcessCommandLine contains "TFTP" or ProcessCommandLine contains "SMB1Protocol" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Client-ProjFS" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Microsoft-Windows-Subsystem-Linux")
